Time Complexity : Relation between input size & Running Time (Operation)
ex. input is N then running will be N times so O(N)

Best Case: Minimum time : omega -^-(1)
Average Case : Average time : thita @(n+1)/2 => @(n)
Worst Case : Max time : big oh O(n)

Always check for worst case

examples:
for(0 to n)
    for(0 to m)
=> O(n*m) all n rows will execute m times

for(0 to n)
for(0 to m)
=>O(n+m) as both loops are individual not depend on each other

here if
for(0 to n) --> n=3
for(0 to m) --> n=2
            -->O(3+2) --> O(5)

But if
for(0 to n) --> n=10^3
for(0 to m) --> n=2
            -->O(10^3) as its clear and more

Compare Time Complexity:

        O(n)    O(n^2)      O(n^3)
n=1       1        1          1
n=2       2        4          8
n=2       3        9          27
n=10^5   10^5     10^10      10^30
         Best      Avg       worst
         Case      case      case

